adopt the following thresholds as a paper-specific reporting convention, calibrated against the E-value literature (VanderWeele & Ding 2017,
Annals of Internal Medicine, and the JAMA Guide to Statistics and Methods entry by Haneuse, VanderWeele & Arterburn 2019). Neither paper
prescribes universal cutoffs; the tiers below are a reporting convenience and
should not be over-interpreted as the literature consensus.
